WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.233 --> 00:00:04.966
Traveling through a forest en route to Coumarine City,

2
00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:07.266
site of Ash's next Kalos Gym battle,

3
00:00:07.333 --> 00:00:10.400
our heroes have met a Pokémon Trainer named Blake.

4
00:00:11.299 --> 00:00:14.966
Right. So your house is really close to this forest, huh?

5
00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:18.833
Yeah. I've been out on a journey for about a year doing some training

6
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.233
and when I smelled all of your delicious food, I figured it was from my house.

7
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.066
It'll be good to get back home.

8
00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.666
-I made a lot, so dig in.

9
00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:30.366
Have as much as you like.

10
00:00:30.433 --> 00:00:32.066
Man, that looks delicious!

11
00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:35.233
By the way. I wanted to ask you about your Pokémon.

12
00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:38.433
It's a Meowstic.

13
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.566
- Meowstic.
- Pikachu.

14
00:00:40.633 --> 00:00:43.566
I can't believe how pretty Meowstic's coat is!

15
00:00:43.633 --> 00:00:46.100
It's beautiful!

16
00:00:46.166 --> 00:00:48.699
Meowstic, the Constraint Pokémon.

17
00:00:48.766 --> 00:00:51.300
When faced with trouble, Meowstic will raise its ears

18
00:00:51.366 --> 00:00:54.500
and create enough psychic power to demolish a ten-ton truck.

19
00:00:54.566 --> 00:00:57.000
Its appearance varies, depending on gender.

20
00:00:57.066 --> 00:01:00.633
Wow. So male and female Meowstic look different!

21
00:01:00.699 --> 00:01:02.766
I totally want to catch one someday!

22
00:01:02.833 --> 00:01:05.733
How do you like it? -Huh?

23
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.266
Mm. It's really delicious!

24
00:01:08.333 --> 00:01:10.933
- Do you think I could have some more?
- Sure thing.

25
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.899
You can have as much as you want. Huh?

26
00:01:14.899 --> 00:01:17.899
Bonnie. You need to eat those veggies, please.

27
00:01:17.966 --> 00:01:20.100
But I don't like these veggies at all!

28
00:01:20.166 --> 00:01:22.466
But veggies are exceptionally nutritious.

29
00:01:22.533 --> 00:01:26.033
You won't grow up to become a first-rate Trainer if you don't eat them now.

30
00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:29.566
Yeah, but you know there are veggies you don't eat 'cause you don't like them.

31
00:01:29.633 --> 00:01:34.333
- Uh, well, that's different.
- Wait a minute! You don't like veggies?

32
00:01:34.399 --> 00:01:36.433
Of course Clemont loves veggies, right?

33
00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:40.333
Uh, that's irrelevant. You finish everything on your plate, Bonnie.

34
00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:43.766
- Hm!
- He's only taking good care of you.

35
00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:48.833
Yeah, but the closer they are, the more they fight. Isn't that the old saying?

36
00:01:48.899 --> 00:01:50.433
I guess so.

37
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.766
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

38
00:01:55.833 --> 00:01:59.500
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

39
00:01:59.566 --> 00:02:02.100
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

40
00:02:02.166 --> 00:02:05.300
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

41
00:02:05.366 --> 00:02:08.366
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

42
00:02:08.433 --> 00:02:11.566
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

43
00:02:11.633 --> 00:02:15.000
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

44
00:02:15.066 --> 00:02:17.766
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

45
00:02:17.833 --> 00:02:19.933
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

46
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.000
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

47
00:02:32.066 --> 00:02:36.200
Pikachu.

48
00:02:36.266 --> 00:02:38.500
Mm. Che. Che.

49
00:02:38.566 --> 00:02:40.200
Che? Pin!

50
00:02:40.266 --> 00:02:43.866
- Che. Che.
- Ew!

51
00:02:44.766 --> 00:02:46.700
Che! Pin?

52
00:02:49.299 --> 00:02:51.900
- Meowstic?
- Che!

53
00:02:51.966 --> 00:02:53.966
- Meow!
- Chespin!

54
00:02:54.033 --> 00:02:57.033
Meowstic was a gift from my father.

55
00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:00.533
Che?

56
00:03:01.433 --> 00:03:02.600
Pin?

57
00:03:02.666 --> 00:03:04.400
- Hey, Chespin!
- Che?

58
00:03:04.466 --> 00:03:07.900
You know you shouldn't be running off like that!

59
00:03:07.966 --> 00:03:10.566
Pin! Che!

60
00:03:10.633 --> 00:03:14.166
- Hey, stop!
- Chespin! Pin! Che! Che!

61
00:03:14.233 --> 00:03:15.933
Pin!

62
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.966
- I got you!
- Ah!

63
00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:20.500
Now, let's go back!

64
00:03:22.299 --> 00:03:24.799
Huh? Uh-oh.

65
00:03:26.833 --> 00:03:29.966
Chespin, do you know which way we came from?

66
00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:30.966
Chespin.

67
00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:34.933
- Of course it's not true!
- Of course it is true.

68
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.966
Right, Bonnie? Bonnie?

69
00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:39.200
- Where did Bonnie go?
- Huh?

70
00:03:39.266 --> 00:03:42.500
- Chespin's gone, too!
- Pik. Pika?

71
00:03:42.566 --> 00:03:47.500
It's the veggies. She must have run off because she didn't want to eat them.

72
00:03:47.566 --> 00:03:51.666
That's bad! Getting lost in this forest could be a really dangerous thing!

73
00:03:51.733 --> 00:03:54.966
There are ponds and cliffs everywhere and wild Beedrill nests, too!

74
00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:56.066
Huh!

75
00:03:56.133 --> 00:04:00.500
Clemont? Ash, where are you?

76
00:04:00.566 --> 00:04:01.933
Hey, Serena?

77
00:04:03.899 --> 00:04:07.933
What do we do? Huh? Maybe this way?

78
00:04:09.966 --> 00:04:12.200
-Huh?

79
00:04:14.366 --> 00:04:17.099
Oh!

80
00:04:17.166 --> 00:04:19.033
- Ah!
- Meowstic! Protect!

81
00:04:19.099 --> 00:04:21.300
Meow!

82
00:04:22.633 --> 00:04:24.933
-Huh?

83
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.466
Ah!

84
00:04:29.933 --> 00:04:31.866
Chespin.

85
00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:37.033
Oh no, we're cornered!

86
00:04:37.099 --> 00:04:38.833
- Use Energy Ball!
- Meowstic!

87
00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.000
- Huh?
- Bonnie!

88
00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.566
- There you are!
- You all right?

89
00:04:47.633 --> 00:04:49.866
Uh, yeah, I guess I'm okay.

90
00:04:49.933 --> 00:04:52.466
- What about Chespin?
- Chespin!

91
00:04:52.533 --> 00:04:55.566
Just like my brother, having trouble fighting Pokémon.

92
00:04:55.633 --> 00:04:58.200
Whoa. The two of you are brothers?

93
00:04:58.266 --> 00:05:00.933
Saving these two was my first priority.

94
00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.599
I was going to chase the Beedrill away after that.

95
00:05:03.666 --> 00:05:06.433
So you're saying my help didn't mean anything?

96
00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:09.000
I'm terribly sorry for getting in your way!

97
00:05:09.066 --> 00:05:12.500
That's not what I meant. It's just that...

98
00:05:12.566 --> 00:05:15.700
I get the feeling those two don't get along so well.

99
00:05:15.766 --> 00:05:19.599
- Even though they're brothers?
- How many times do I have to tell you?

100
00:05:19.666 --> 00:05:22.966
- Don't go off alone!
- But the thing is...

101
00:05:23.033 --> 00:05:25.933
Wait a minute. Maybe there's an explanation.

102
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.700
It doesn't matter! If something had happened to her--

103
00:05:28.766 --> 00:05:31.433
Let's drop it. Bonnie and Chespin are okay

104
00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:33.500
and that's the thing that really matters!

105
00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:37.599
- Pika.
- Uh, thank you for saving my sister.

106
00:05:37.666 --> 00:05:41.766
Of course. First things first, I think we should treat her injuries.

107
00:05:41.833 --> 00:05:43.133
Huh.

108
00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:46.766
Our house is close by and we can treat you there.

109
00:05:46.833 --> 00:05:48.833
Thanks very much!

110
00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:51.666
- How are you feeling, Bonnie?
- Hm!

111
00:05:51.733 --> 00:05:54.233
- Huh?
- But, Bonnie!

112
00:05:58.266 --> 00:06:00.633
- This is your house?
- Right.

113
00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:02.666
Are you sure we're not intruding?

114
00:06:02.733 --> 00:06:06.166
- Not at all.
- Pin! Che!

115
00:06:06.233 --> 00:06:08.166
We're back!

116
00:06:12.566 --> 00:06:14.733
It's my Blake and my Heath!

117
00:06:16.099 --> 00:06:18.900
What a relief! Thank goodness you're both all right!

118
00:06:18.966 --> 00:06:21.166
- We're fine, Mom.
- Good to be home.

119
00:06:21.233 --> 00:06:25.133
Since you've been on the road, you've hardly ever called your mother.

120
00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.533
- I've been so worried!
- I'm sorry, Mom.

121
00:06:27.599 --> 00:06:29.900
But as you can see, we're doing great!

122
00:06:29.966 --> 00:06:35.366
Huh! Hm. And look here, I see that you've brought several guests with you.

123
00:06:35.433 --> 00:06:39.966
Right. She's injured, so I invited them all back so we can treat her.

124
00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:44.133
Oh, that's terrible! Hold on and I'll get the first aid kit.

125
00:06:46.633 --> 00:06:48.833
There. All set.

126
00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:51.400
- Thank you!
- Na-na-na-na!

127
00:06:51.466 --> 00:06:54.400
- Bonnie, does it hurt?
- No.

128
00:06:54.466 --> 00:06:57.833
Thank you for taking such good care of my sister.

129
00:06:58.966 --> 00:07:02.700
- Mah!
- My sons used to play all day long.

130
00:07:02.766 --> 00:07:07.099
They were always outdoors having lots of adventures and getting scratched up!

131
00:07:07.166 --> 00:07:08.566
Mom, come on.

132
00:07:08.633 --> 00:07:11.133
That was a long time ago.

133
00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:17.533
Hi there. I'm so glad you've finally decided to come back home.

134
00:07:17.599 --> 00:07:19.466
You seem to have matured a bit.

135
00:07:19.533 --> 00:07:21.833
- Hi there, Dad!
- Of course we've grown.

136
00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:24.733
Yup. We've been training on our journey for a year now.

137
00:07:24.799 --> 00:07:27.766
I'm not the same as I was. Don't you think so, Meowstic?

138
00:07:27.833 --> 00:07:29.266
Meow! Meow!

139
00:07:29.333 --> 00:07:32.766
And I too worked as hard as I possibly could this whole year, too.

140
00:07:32.833 --> 00:07:34.266
Meowstic.

141
00:07:34.333 --> 00:07:37.900
All right, I think the moment has come for you to take part

142
00:07:37.966 --> 00:07:40.966
in what has been a family tradition for generations. A trial.

143
00:07:41.033 --> 00:07:43.000
- Huh?
- What's that mean?

144
00:07:43.066 --> 00:07:44.066
Pika?

145
00:07:44.133 --> 00:07:46.900
There comes a time when our family must decide

146
00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:49.366
who will inherit our house and property.

147
00:07:49.433 --> 00:07:52.066
In order to do that, we conduct a sort of trial.

148
00:07:52.133 --> 00:07:55.233
- So, then that means...
- That's my brother and me.

149
00:07:55.299 --> 00:07:58.799
Correct. I'm sure you learned a lot during your travels,

150
00:07:58.866 --> 00:08:01.166
so let's see how strong you've both become.

151
00:08:01.233 --> 00:08:03.200
All right! I've been waiting for this!

152
00:08:03.266 --> 00:08:06.166
- No matter what the test, I'll win!
- Meow!

153
00:08:06.233 --> 00:08:09.266
- I have no intention of losing.
- Meowstic!

154
00:08:09.333 --> 00:08:11.799
Now. The heir will be chosen by a method

155
00:08:11.866 --> 00:08:14.766
that's been passed down from generation to generation.

156
00:08:14.833 --> 00:08:17.566
- That sounds like a long time.
- Na-na?

157
00:08:17.633 --> 00:08:20.633
I wonder what kind of method he's talking about.

158
00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:23.166
The method? Hm.

159
00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:26.133
We will have a treasure hunt.

160
00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:28.633
- Have a treasure hunt?
- Pika?

161
00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:32.333
Now, I have hidden the treasure somewhere on the property.

162
00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:35.266
He who will be my successor must find it.

163
00:08:35.333 --> 00:08:38.433
Yes. It doesn't matter what the treasure is,

164
00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:41.266
- 'cause I'm going to find it first!
- Hm!

165
00:08:41.333 --> 00:08:44.133
I realize the search area is rather big.

166
00:08:44.199 --> 00:08:47.266
Therefore, you will both be permitted an assistant.

167
00:08:47.333 --> 00:08:49.300
Assistant?

168
00:08:49.366 --> 00:08:51.933
I'd like Ash. Will you help me out, please?

169
00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:55.133
Huh? Really? I'm happy to help any way I can.

170
00:08:55.199 --> 00:08:57.666
In that case, then I want to help Heath!

171
00:08:57.733 --> 00:08:59.066
- Huh?
- Huh?

172
00:08:59.133 --> 00:09:03.066
After all, Heath saved me. It's the least I can do!

173
00:09:03.133 --> 00:09:05.800
- Will you help us too, Serena?
- You want me?

174
00:09:05.866 --> 00:09:09.800
Yeah and my big brother can help Blake with Ash. Hm!

175
00:09:09.866 --> 00:09:11.233
Hm!

176
00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:14.433
- Okay! We'll split into two teams.
- Sounds good!

177
00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:16.800
- Let's win! Okay, Heath?
- Right.

178
00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:21.433
And when you've finally located the treasure,

179
00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:25.366
then you will bring it back to me. If it truly is the treasure,

180
00:09:25.433 --> 00:09:27.766
the test will end right then and there.

181
00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:32.333
- Let's go! I'm not about to lose!
- Meow, Meowstic!

182
00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:33.766
- Come on!
- Meowstic!

183
00:09:33.833 --> 00:09:37.233
Che!

184
00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:38.666
- Chespin!
- Che?

185
00:09:38.733 --> 00:09:44.199
- No, this way!
- Eh, eh? Che? Che! Che!

186
00:09:44.266 --> 00:09:46.566
Che! Chespin!

187
00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:52.533
So, any idea where the treasure is, Blake?

188
00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:56.633
Not really. I think we should check everything that looks suspicious.

189
00:09:56.699 --> 00:09:58.400
Okay.

190
00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:02.400
- Hm.
- Chespin!

191
00:10:02.466 --> 00:10:07.600
Hey, Blake, you don't get along that well with your brother, do you?

192
00:10:07.666 --> 00:10:11.333
See, I just don't want to lose to him, that's all,

193
00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:14.000
even though we used to be really close.

194
00:10:14.066 --> 00:10:19.166
Our family used to go picnicking together on a nearby hill when I was a little kid.

195
00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:21.666
Espurr!

196
00:10:21.733 --> 00:10:24.866
One day, my dad gave us two Espurr

197
00:10:24.933 --> 00:10:28.100
and it wasn't long before they evolved into Meowstic,

198
00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:32.133
which was also when my brother and I started to butt heads.

199
00:10:32.199 --> 00:10:34.166
Meow! Meowstic!

200
00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:36.833
- Meowstic!
- Psychic, go!

201
00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:39.666
Meow, Meow!

202
00:10:39.733 --> 00:10:42.833
- Energy Ball, once more!
- Meow! Meow!

203
00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:45.833
No, you're doing it wrong! If you want to make the most

204
00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:49.233
out of Meowstic's powers, the first thing you need to do is--

205
00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:52.633
Knock it off! I'll battle any way that I want to!

206
00:10:52.699 --> 00:10:55.300
So get off of my back and keep off!

207
00:10:55.366 --> 00:10:58.133
I'm old enough to take care of myself

208
00:10:58.199 --> 00:11:01.400
and I've got to prove that to the rest of my family!

209
00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:07.733
Having a brother or sister is not all that easy, is it?

210
00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:10.466
- Hey, Clemont.
- Che?

211
00:11:10.533 --> 00:11:13.900
You're right. I nag Bonnie sometimes.

212
00:11:13.966 --> 00:11:16.966
The thing is, I never really mean to.

213
00:11:17.033 --> 00:11:20.400
- You don't do that! Don't be silly!
- But, Ash.

214
00:11:20.466 --> 00:11:23.699
You got angry with Bonnie because you were worried about her, right?

215
00:11:23.766 --> 00:11:26.066
I'm sure Bonnie knows that's the real reason.

216
00:11:26.133 --> 00:11:29.166
- You really think so?
- No doubt about it!

217
00:11:29.233 --> 00:11:31.533
She knows you're only trying to take care of her.

218
00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:33.066
- Pikachu!
- Chespin.

219
00:11:33.133 --> 00:11:36.000
Hm. I guess so. Thanks!

220
00:11:36.066 --> 00:11:38.500
Who's that Pokémon?

221
00:11:43.066 --> 00:11:44.866
It's Meowstic!

222
00:11:49.066 --> 00:11:52.000
Wow! This is such a pretty room!

223
00:11:52.066 --> 00:11:54.800
All right, I'll go and search the room next door.

224
00:11:54.866 --> 00:11:58.000
- Leave this room to us!
- Na-na-na!

225
00:11:59.133 --> 00:12:01.333
Hm.

226
00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:03.933
Huh? Look! Is that it?

227
00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:08.666
Huh? Uh, I didn't hear what you said.

228
00:12:08.733 --> 00:12:12.666
- Meow.
- Hey, Heath, is something the matter?

229
00:12:12.733 --> 00:12:15.733
- Um... It's nothing.
- You were frowning.

230
00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:17.900
Your forehead got all scrunchy right here.

231
00:12:17.966 --> 00:12:19.033
Uh...

232
00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:22.300
I've seen that before. Clemont does it when he's thinking.

233
00:12:22.366 --> 00:12:24.933
His forehead gets all smooshed and wrinkly.

234
00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:26.633
Huh?

235
00:12:26.699 --> 00:12:29.633
You really care about your brother a lot, don't you?

236
00:12:29.699 --> 00:12:33.500
Oh, no, I don't! He always nags me and gets mad!

237
00:12:33.566 --> 00:12:36.500
Know what? I wish you were my brother instead!

238
00:12:36.566 --> 00:12:39.566
- You know, I'm the same way, too.
- Huh?

239
00:12:39.633 --> 00:12:41.800
Blake doesn't like me very much either.

240
00:12:41.866 --> 00:12:45.533
- Do you guys fight?
- Yeah, we do. I worry about him.

241
00:12:45.599 --> 00:12:48.500
So I'm always giving him advice, which he doesn't like.

242
00:12:49.966 --> 00:12:51.666
Listen. I'm going to become

243
00:12:51.733 --> 00:12:54.900
a better and stronger Pokémon Trainer than you'll ever be!

244
00:12:59.266 --> 00:13:02.733
It's not like I purposely want to pick a fight or anything.

245
00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:05.933
Okay. Does that mean you're saying you're not mad at Blake?

246
00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:09.333
Of course I'm not mad! He's my precious little brother.

247
00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:12.966
- So what about the treasure hunt?
- I don't want to fight with my brother.

248
00:13:13.033 --> 00:13:16.199
But Blake won't like it if I end up losing on purpose.

249
00:13:16.266 --> 00:13:18.366
I'm going to take him on fair and square.

250
00:13:18.433 --> 00:13:20.666
Okay, I see.

251
00:13:22.966 --> 00:13:26.666
- None of these are the treasure.
- Huh! I don't get it!

252
00:13:26.733 --> 00:13:29.166
We already searched the entire house.

253
00:13:29.233 --> 00:13:30.766
- Pika!
- Pin! Pin!

254
00:13:30.833 --> 00:13:34.699
So let's see. I guess I'll have to give you a hint.

255
00:13:34.766 --> 00:13:37.666
The treasure is currently not inside the house.

256
00:13:37.733 --> 00:13:40.966
- Huh?
- Then it's got to be somewhere outside.

257
00:13:41.033 --> 00:13:44.266
Aw! That's why we couldn't find it!

258
00:13:44.333 --> 00:13:46.333
Think about this and remember.

259
00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:49.199
The treasure has something to do with the both of you.

260
00:13:49.266 --> 00:13:51.066
Huh!

261
00:13:54.133 --> 00:13:56.233
Hm.

262
00:13:56.300 --> 00:13:59.599
Hey, Blake? Does that hint remind you of anything?

263
00:13:59.666 --> 00:14:02.800
The both of us. Let me see!

264
00:14:02.866 --> 00:14:05.266
I'll never forget what we saw today!

265
00:14:05.333 --> 00:14:09.000
Me neither! I'll always remember, even when I'm all grown up!

266
00:14:09.066 --> 00:14:11.366
Of course. It must be!

267
00:14:11.433 --> 00:14:14.133
- Where are we going?

268
00:14:14.199 --> 00:14:17.433
The secret place my brother and I found when we were little kids!

269
00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:20.000
Some really rare flowers bloom there!

270
00:14:22.166 --> 00:14:24.266
- Hm.
- Pe.

271
00:14:24.333 --> 00:14:25.966
What's that?

272
00:14:26.033 --> 00:14:28.666
- Huh? It's a Venipede!
- Oh!

273
00:14:28.733 --> 00:14:31.466
Pe, pe, pe!

274
00:14:31.533 --> 00:14:36.900
Pe, pe, pe, pe! Pe, pe, pe!

275
00:14:39.933 --> 00:14:42.900
How beautiful! Thank you so much!

276
00:14:44.433 --> 00:14:47.366
We made Mom and Dad really happy that day.

277
00:14:47.433 --> 00:14:49.766
It's got to be those flowers!

278
00:14:52.966 --> 00:14:54.566
It's Heath!

279
00:14:54.633 --> 00:14:58.000
Hey there, Blake. You remembered, too.

280
00:14:58.066 --> 00:15:01.800
Yeah. This is where I thought they'd be.

281
00:15:01.866 --> 00:15:08.000
You mean the flowers. They're in bloom.

282
00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:11.133
- Oh!
- I'm surprised you remembered.

283
00:15:11.199 --> 00:15:13.199
- You, too.

284
00:15:13.266 --> 00:15:15.566
Huh? Hm.

285
00:15:16.733 --> 00:15:19.033
Those flowers are the treasure?

286
00:15:19.099 --> 00:15:20.633
Knowing Dad, yes.

287
00:15:20.699 --> 00:15:23.400
- Exploud!
- What's that?

288
00:15:27.333 --> 00:15:30.066
An Exploud!

289
00:15:30.133 --> 00:15:32.766
- It's using Hyper Voice!

290
00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:40.666
Chespin, Pin!

291
00:15:40.733 --> 00:15:43.266
- All right, Chespin, Pin Missile!
- Pin!

292
00:15:43.333 --> 00:15:47.266
Chespin!

293
00:15:48.833 --> 00:15:51.333
- Pikachu, let's chase it away!
- Pika!

294
00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:53.500
- Hold on!
- We'll do it!

295
00:15:53.566 --> 00:15:54.766
- Huh?
- Pika?

296
00:15:56.133 --> 00:15:58.166
- Meow!
- Ready, Heath?

297
00:15:58.233 --> 00:16:01.933
- Yes, all set. Meowstic, use Scratch!
- Meow!

298
00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:04.533
- Meowstic, use Scratch, too!
- Meow!

299
00:16:05.433 --> 00:16:08.566
Meow!

300
00:16:12.133 --> 00:16:14.599
- Meow!
- Scratch, once more!

301
00:16:14.666 --> 00:16:16.099
Meowstic!

302
00:16:22.699 --> 00:16:24.099
- Protect!
- Meow!

303
00:16:30.099 --> 00:16:32.133
Blake, don't be so hasty!

304
00:16:32.199 --> 00:16:35.633
- Right. I'll be careful.
- Then you've got the attack.

305
00:16:37.699 --> 00:16:41.000
- Meowstic, use Psychic!
- Use Energy Ball!

306
00:16:42.433 --> 00:16:44.866
Meow!

307
00:16:44.933 --> 00:16:48.099
Meowstic!

308
00:16:50.599 --> 00:16:52.666
- Awesome!
- Pika!

309
00:16:52.733 --> 00:16:55.199
- Yay, yay!
- Wow, just like brothers!

310
00:16:55.266 --> 00:16:57.966
- Great coordination!
- Know what I'm thinking?

311
00:16:58.033 --> 00:16:59.500
Brings back memories.

312
00:17:04.866 --> 00:17:07.466
- Che!

313
00:17:08.866 --> 00:17:11.599
Oh!

314
00:17:11.666 --> 00:17:13.200
Bonnie! Hm.

315
00:17:14.399 --> 00:17:16.399
- No, Clemont!
- No, Bonnie!

316
00:17:16.466 --> 00:17:18.200
Huh?

317
00:17:19.866 --> 00:17:21.533
Enough!

318
00:17:25.633 --> 00:17:27.566
- But how?
- Pika?

319
00:17:27.633 --> 00:17:31.033
Very well done. Thanks a lot, Exploud. Now return.

320
00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:35.133
- What's going on?
- I don't understand what just happened.

321
00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:38.300
Does it mean that Exploud is your Pokémon, Dad?

322
00:17:38.366 --> 00:17:42.800
That's right. I instructed Exploud to wait for you two here.

323
00:17:42.866 --> 00:17:44.733
Why would you do something like that?

324
00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:48.300
Because I truly wanted both my sons to remember,

325
00:17:48.366 --> 00:17:52.466
back to the time you battled as a team, shoulder to shoulder.

326
00:17:52.533 --> 00:17:53.733
Hm?

327
00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:56.899
- Hm!
- Huh.

328
00:17:58.266 --> 00:18:01.500
So you chased away the Venipede together, did you?

329
00:18:01.566 --> 00:18:04.399
The bond you two share is our family treasure.

330
00:18:04.466 --> 00:18:07.433
I hope you'll always remember and cherish that.

331
00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:09.000
I won't forget it, Dad!

332
00:18:09.066 --> 00:18:12.566
I'll always remember it, too, even after I'm all grown up!

333
00:18:13.633 --> 00:18:17.266
That timing of the Energy Ball you used was perfect.

334
00:18:17.333 --> 00:18:19.866
Well, I couldn't have done it without your help.

335
00:18:23.033 --> 00:18:26.866
The true treasure is to be found within your hearts.

336
00:18:26.933 --> 00:18:28.966
I want you both to remember this.

337
00:18:29.033 --> 00:18:30.700
Oh, Dad.

338
00:18:30.766 --> 00:18:33.466
I know I made you worry. Sorry.

339
00:18:33.533 --> 00:18:37.466
Sorry? There's no need for regret now that you're home!

340
00:18:37.533 --> 00:18:40.000
It's so great that those two made up.

341
00:18:40.066 --> 00:18:43.333
- Pikachu.
- So what about the two of you?

342
00:18:43.399 --> 00:18:45.033
Huh? Uh...

343
00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:46.733
Hm.

344
00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:49.933
I know I'm not the most dependable brother,

345
00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:53.766
but there will never be a moment when I stop caring about you!

346
00:18:53.833 --> 00:18:56.933
Believe it or not, that's why I nag you from time to time.

347
00:18:57.000 --> 00:19:02.066
Uh-uh. Clemont, I'm sorry too. I should have told you before I left.

348
00:19:02.133 --> 00:19:05.000
I'll even eat every one of my veggies.

349
00:19:05.066 --> 00:19:07.333
So will you always be my big brother?

350
00:19:07.399 --> 00:19:11.833
I'll be your brother forever! You're my little sister and I love you.

351
00:19:11.899 --> 00:19:15.833
Hm!

352
00:19:17.166 --> 00:19:20.333
- All's well that ends well, you know?
- Yeah.

353
00:19:20.399 --> 00:19:23.800
- Dad, you're the best!
- Meowstic.

354
00:19:25.399 --> 00:19:28.333
Che.

355
00:19:28.399 --> 00:19:31.333
Meow.

356
00:19:31.399 --> 00:19:36.700
Che, Che, Chespin, Che, Che! Pin?

357
00:19:36.766 --> 00:19:39.200
- Meowstic!
- Meowstic. Meow, Meow.

358
00:19:40.233 --> 00:19:41.700
Chespin?

359
00:19:41.766 --> 00:19:45.200
- Huh!
- Those Meowstic are...

360
00:19:45.266 --> 00:19:49.500
They haven't seen each other since Blake and I went our separate ways.

361
00:19:49.566 --> 00:19:52.033
They've always been very close.

362
00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:55.200
Meowstic, from now on you two will always be together.

363
00:19:55.266 --> 00:19:57.200
Meow! Meowstic, Meow, Meow!

364
00:19:57.266 --> 00:19:59.433
Meowstic! Meow!

365
00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:03.166
Che!

366
00:20:03.233 --> 00:20:05.700
Come on, Chespin, cheer up!

367
00:20:05.766 --> 00:20:09.800
I'll bake you some Poké Puffs. You'll find true love someday soon.

368
00:20:16.233 --> 00:20:19.133
Thanks! Take care of yourselves on your journey!

369
00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:21.000
Be sure to come back again some time.

370
00:20:21.066 --> 00:20:23.300
You bet and thanks to both of you!

371
00:20:23.366 --> 00:20:25.233
Take care of each other!

372
00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:26.833
Bye-bye, then!

373
00:20:26.899 --> 00:20:29.000
I'm glad you're a team again!

374
00:20:29.066 --> 00:20:32.333
"The closer they are, the more they fight."

375
00:20:32.399 --> 00:20:35.000
Two pairs of siblings were able to make amends

376
00:20:35.066 --> 00:20:37.233
and reaffirm the bonds between them.

377
00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:41.700
And so, with Clemont and Bonnie's bickering sure to bring them even closer,

378
00:20:41.766 --> 00:20:46.633
it's on to Coumarine City, as our heroes' journey continues!
